{
    "_doc": "The trades of a town square's market stalls and the marketplace hall's stalls (world/marketStalls.js). Each stall is one trader: it sells only its trade's goods, out of the town market's real stock (settlement.market) at the market's own prices, and its keeper buys back only goods of its trade (goods + buys). A stall's trade is drawn once per stall by a hash of the world seed, the town and the stall's place, weighted by the trade's weight x its culture's multiplier x the land around the town (land: terrain class shares) x how well the market is stocked in its goods, never two alike in one square while another trade is open; it is kept on the settlement (settlement.stallTrades) and only drawn again if the town no longer allows it (tier, type, culture, water). tiers: the town's wealth tiers (world/settlementWealth.js standing) the trade sets up in; routeTiers: tiers it also sets up in when traders bring goods in (market.trade.in >= routeIn); minType: the smallest settlement with the trade; needsWater: only by the sea, a lake or a river; minWares: goods of its own the market must have in stock (>= 1 unit) for the trade to set up; cultures: weight multipliers by culture (0 bars it); stall: the stall's name ('Marta's Fish Stall'); art: its counter wares and side props (data/townProps.json stallArt; defaults to the trade id); cries: what its keeper calls out ({good} is one of the wares in stock, {town} the town); artVariants: other looks the stall wears by what it has in stock today, the first whose goods it has at least min (and at most max) of in stock (world/marketStalls.js artFor): the greengrocer heaped with fruit after the harvest, with roots and cabbages through the winter.",
